ube.<\/p>","rating":0,"date":1539033341,"modified_date":1539033341,"status":"public"}]},{"commentid":839006,"locale":"en","context":"guide","contextid":95160,"parentid":null,"author":{"userid":4211657,"username":"Water Ski","unique_username":"waterski","join_date":1667324887,"image":{"id":2773910,"guid":"ysidWewYZglGInOY","mini":"https:\/\/guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com\/igi\/ysidWewYZglGInOY.mini","thumbnail":"https:\/\/guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com\/igi\/ysidWewYZglGInOY.thumbnail","original":"https:\/\/guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com\/igi\/ysidWewYZglGInOY.full"},"reputation":5,"url":"https:\/\/www.ifixit.com\/User\/4211657\/Water+Ski","teams":[]},"title":"2003-2007 Honda Accord Serpentine Belt Replacement","text_raw":"Just did this replacement last night. Bought the belt from O'Reilly and rented the serpentine belt toolset. It didn't come with a 14 mm socket, but I was able to borrow one they had. Fairly easy to remove the belt, but putting it on, especially in the dark, was nontrivial. I recommend doing in the daylight.\n\nBe sure that the tensioner springs pushes back while you're starting; it may need to be replaced too.\n\nI had to really reach my arm all the way down to get the new belt on, and then be creative to get it around all the right pieces. Perhaps a longer socket would have helped for being able to push the tensioner back and still have space to work with the belt.","text_rendered":"<p>Just did this replacement last night. Bought the belt from O'Reilly and rented the serpentine belt toolset. It didn't come with a 14 mm socket, but I was able to borrow one they had. Fairly easy to remove the belt, but putting it on, especially in the dark, was nontrivial. I recommend doing in the daylight.<\/p>\n\n<p>Be sure that the tensioner springs pushes back while you're starting; it may need to be replaced too.<\/p>\n\n<p>I had to really reach my arm all the way down to get the new belt on, and then be creative to get it around all the right pieces. Perhaps a longer socket would have helped for being able to push the tensioner back and still have space to work with the belt.<\/p>","rating":0,"date":1667325304,"modified_date":0,"status":"public","replies":[]}],"category":"2003-2007 Honda Accord","url":"https:\/\/www.ifixit.com\/Guide\/2003+2004+2005+2006+2007+Honda+Accord+Serpentine+Belt+Replacement\/95160","patrol_threshold":30000,"can_edit":true,"favorited":false,"author":{"userid":2012381,"username":"eCuration","unique_username":"e_curation","join_date":1495219750,"image":{"id":1127364,"guid":"vxmZa1BuxNTWWnGf","mini":"https:\/\/guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com\/igi\/vxmZa1BuxNTWWnGf.mini","thumbnail":"https:\/\/guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com\/igi\/vxmZa1BuxNTWWnGf.thumbnail","140x105":"https:\/\/guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com\/igi\/vxmZa1BuxNTWWnGf.140x105","200x150":"https:\/\/guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com\/igi\/vxmZa1BuxNTWWnGf.200x150","standard":"https:\/\/guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com\/igi\/vxmZa1BuxNTWWnGf.standard","440x330":"https:\/\/guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com\/igi\/vxmZa1BuxNTWWnGf.440x330","medium":"https:\/\/guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com\/igi\/vxmZa1BuxNTWWnGf.medium","original":"https:\/\/guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com\/igi\/vxmZa1BuxNTWWnGf.full"},"reputation":478744,"url":"https:\/\/www.ifixit.com\/User\/2012381\/eCuration","teams":[1]},"langid":"en","unreviewed_machine_translation":false,"featured_documentid":null,"intro_video_url":"http:\/\/www.youtube.com\/watch?v=JAQDYMfCcc0","intro_video":{"embedid":470,"url":"http:\/\/www.youtube.com\/watch?v=JAQDYMfCcc0","width":1280,"height":720,"title":"2003-2012 Honda Accord serpentine belt replacement","type":"RICH","provider_url":"https:\/\/www.youtube.com\/","html":"<iframe width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" src=\"https:\/\/www.youtube.com\/embed\/JAQDYMfCcc0?feature=oembed\" frameborder=\"0\" allowfullscreen><\/iframe>","provider_name":"YouTube","author_url":"https:\/\/www.youtube.com\/user\/NutzAboutBolts2","author_name":"NutzAboutBolts","cache_age":null,"version":"1.0"},"completed":fal